Dawit Bekele requests a working local portfolio: one scroll-driven story in 3D, guided decisions. No publishing, hosting, domain, legal work or sending mail. No additional skills, external visual assets, photos, slides, testimonials, blog/chat/form/translation. System fonts and own geometry only. Build dependencies installed offline; no new packages or assets downloaded during this build.

Confirmed facts and permissions: docs/story/facts.md, including the user's detailed confirmations and build fact audit. Those override the original material. Source folder has only four read profile markdown files; no private correspondence encountered. Use exactly six requested work pieces. Scope availability to measured Order API 99.98% over 26 months; never zero downtime. Team on-call result uses we, nine people, 85→22/week over about a year. Credit ferry's former-colleague creator and Dawit's maintenance/cutover command. Lumen only permitted one-line LinkedIn description. Any Kestrel drawings are own labelled illustrations, never internal assets.

## Decisions already made

- World explicitly accepted after user scrolled site and gallery: whole sheet, WHOLE.sheet. Quote in concepts.md. Never reopen world choice without request.
- User said “Keep everything else as it is.” Honour existing Night/Swing appearance; do not ask for the same decision again. Whole-site Night/Daylight/Blueprint and Swing/Fold/Slide previews/captures are available for optional inspection; defaults retained.
- Storyboard explicitly approved: “Yes to the storyboard in docs/story/storyboard.md. Please build it.” Approval appended to storyboard.md.
- No final opening/closing wording chosen yet. New candidates must remain unapplied until answer.

## What exists

App in site/ (scaffold root rejected because it contains installed engine). Run:

```bash
cd site
npm run dev -- --hostname 127.0.0.1
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:3000. Existing production build can use npm run start. The tool environment's sandbox commands do not share a reachable persistent loopback server; verified browser checks start server and browser in the same command. Do not promise a server still running across tool calls. User can start it in their terminal.

- `/`: all seven sheet chapters, main navigation/rail, six native project-detail dialogs, contact and working CV link. Entire factual story and full work detail are server-rendered for no-JS/no-WebGL. All stitch/ files and main app/page.tsx remain original library components; verified by directory diff.
- `/cv`: curated confirmed CV, responsive, printable with A4 CSS; uses functional descriptions where a formal title was not confirmed. Lumen remains one line.
- `/cv/download`: attachment Dawit-Bekele-CV.html, self-contained HTML with shared content/style, no JS/font/image/stylesheet dependencies. Page and attachment use content/cv.ts; renderer lib/cv.ts escapes text. Browser Print/Save as PDF instruction; not a promised pre-generated PDF product.
